1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,200
In Antarctica's freezing Dry Valleys,

2
00:00:02,306 --> 00:00:04,424
a five-story waterfall pours blood-red

3
00:00:04,454 --> 00:00:06,545
straight out of solid glacier ice.

4
00:00:06,723 --> 00:00:08,618
For decades, nobody knew what fed

5
00:00:08,648 --> 00:00:10,345
Taylor Glacier's Blood Falls.

6
00:00:11,098 --> 00:00:13,500
Today, we know the color comes from chemistry:

7
00:00:13,611 --> 00:00:15,796
salty, iron-rich water hits the air

8
00:00:15,826 --> 00:00:17,287
and instantly rusts.

9
00:00:17,496 --> 00:00:18,589
Deep under the ice sits

10
00:00:18,619 --> 00:00:20,857
a trapped reservoir of hyper-salty brine—

11
00:00:20,944 --> 00:00:22,789
likely ancient seawater sealed off

12
00:00:22,819 --> 00:00:24,195
as the glacier advanced,

13
00:00:24,319 --> 00:00:26,932
though its full history remains under investigation.

14
00:00:27,167 --> 00:00:28,493
Rust explains the color.

15
00:00:29,237 --> 00:00:31,560
What surprised researchers in 2026

16
00:00:31,590 --> 00:00:32,357
was what they pulled

17
00:00:32,387 --> 00:00:33,749
from the freezing red mud.

18
00:00:33,963 --> 00:00:37,162
Testing 167 ice, sediment, air,

19
00:00:37,359 --> 00:00:39,297
and ocean samples across the region,

20
00:00:39,327 --> 00:00:41,314
a field team uncovered a hidden community

21
00:00:41,344 --> 00:00:43,771
of marine microbes right at the red outflow.

22
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:47,167
Under the microscope were tiny ocean algae like diatoms,

23
00:00:47,267 --> 00:00:49,405
alongside single-celled marine drifters—

24
00:00:49,542 --> 00:00:51,680
living clues of past ocean connections,

25
00:00:51,792 --> 00:00:53,230
miles from open sea.

26
00:00:53,475 --> 00:00:55,895
Now, that doesn't prove these exact organisms

27
00:00:55,925 --> 00:00:57,311
stayed trapped beneath the ice

28
00:00:57,341 --> 00:00:58,665
for millions of years.

29
00:00:59,446 --> 00:01:01,342
Scientists are still piecing together

30
00:01:01,372 --> 00:01:02,404
how they got there.

31
00:01:02,743 --> 00:01:04,189
Blood Falls isn't bleeding.

32
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:06,752
It's a leaking subglacial vault—

33
00:01:06,842 --> 00:01:10,098
showing that even beneath 400 meters of Antarctic ice,

34
00:01:10,225 --> 00:01:12,497
Earth holds unexpected signs of life.
